  "id": "accessory-symptoms",
  "term": "accessory symptoms",
  "definition": "Accessory symptoms are additional symptoms that count alongside the core separation-distress symptoms when determining whether prolonged grief disorder is present. In the source, they are the accompanying grief-related symptoms that must be present to a functionally impairing degree, with the required number differing between ICD-11 and DSM-5-TR approaches.",
